<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
	Hardened-runtime entitlements for the notarized macOS build. Each of these is here
	for a reason; do not add more to make an error go away without recording why.

	- network.client       — the wrapped web app talks to the Anthers API. Without it
	                         every request fails once the hardened runtime is on.
	- allow-jit +
	  allow-unsigned-
	  executable-memory    — WKWebView JITs JavaScript. The hardened runtime blocks
	                         writable-executable memory by default, which takes the
	                         webview (i.e. the entire app) down with it.

	NOT included, deliberately:
	- disable-library-validation — no native sidecars are bundled, so nothing here
	  loads external dylibs beyond the system webview stack. If the app ever bundles
	  one that links shared libraries, this entitlement is where that would have to
	  change, and it should be a conscious decision rather than a copied-in default.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>com.apple.security.network.client</key>
	<true/>
	<key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-jit</key>
	<true/>
	<key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-unsigned-executable-memory</key>
	<true/>
</dict>
</plist>
